Power generation plants
🔌 Generation → 621.31

12 distinct models including thermal (coal), nuclear, hydroelectric, natural gas, 
diesel, solar, wind, biomass, geothermal, tidal, wave, and waste-to-energy facilities.


1. THERMAL (COAL)
   Conversion: chemical energy in coal -> heat -> steam -> turbine -> generator
   Cycle: Rankine
   Key vars: calorific value (kJ/kg), steam P/T, boiler efficiency, heat rate (kJ/kWh)
   Fundamentals: combustion, heat transfer, superheated steam, condenser vacuum

2. NUCLEAR
   Conversion: fission heat -> steam -> turbine -> generator
   Cycle: Rankine (PWR/BWR) or Brayton (some advanced)
   Key vars: enrichment, burnup (GWd/t), thermal power, capacity factor
   Fundamentals: neutron chain reaction, moderator, control rods, decay heat

3. HYDROELECTRIC
   Conversion: gravitational PE of water -> kinetic -> turbine -> generator
   Key vars: head H (m), flow Q (m3/s), density, turbine efficiency
   Power: P = ρ g Q H η
   Fundamentals: Bernoulli, impulse vs reaction turbines (Pelton/Francis/Kaplan)

4. NATURAL GAS
   Conversion: chemical energy -> combustion -> gas turbine (+ steam bottoming)
   Cycle: Brayton + Rankine (combined cycle)
   Key vars: LHV, pressure ratio, TIT, heat rate, CCGT efficiency (~55-64%)
   Fundamentals: compressor work, expansion work, HRSG

5. DIESEL
   Conversion: chemical energy -> ICE combustion -> crankshaft -> generator
   Cycle: Diesel (compression ignition)
   Key vars: compression ratio, specific fuel consumption (g/kWh), load factor
   Fundamentals: four-stroke, air-fuel ratio, governor speed control

6. SOLAR PV
   Conversion: photons -> electron-hole pairs -> DC current -> inverter -> AC
   Key vars: irradiance (W/m2), cell efficiency, fill factor, temperature coeff
   Fundamentals: photovoltaic effect, I-V curve, MPPT, inverter clipping

7. WIND
   Conversion: kinetic energy of air -> rotor torque -> generator
   Power: P = ½ ρ A v³ Cp  (Betz limit Cp ≤ 16/27)
   Key vars: wind speed v, rotor area A, tip-speed ratio, capacity factor
   Fundamentals: lift/drag on blades, cut-in / rated / cut-out speeds

8. BIOMASS
   Conversion: chemical energy in organic matter -> heat/steam or gasification
   Key vars: moisture content, calorific value, combustion temp, ash content
   Fundamentals: similar to coal Rankine or syngas + engine/turbine

9. GEOTHERMAL
   Conversion: Earth's internal heat -> steam or binary fluid -> turbine
   Types: dry steam, flash, binary (ORC)
   Key vars: reservoir temp, enthalpy, well flow, brine chemistry
   Fundamentals: hydrothermal systems, Organic Rankine Cycle for low-T

10. TIDAL
    Conversion: potential/kinetic energy of tides -> turbine
    Key vars: tidal range, basin area, flow velocity, cycle period (~12.4 h)
    Fundamentals: gravitational pull of Moon/Sun, barrage vs stream turbines

11. WAVE
    Conversion: wave orbital motion / heave / surge -> hydraulic or linear gen
    Key vars: wave height Hs, period T, power flux (~kW/m of crest)
    Fundamentals: Airy/Stokes waves, oscillating water column, point absorbers

12. WASTE-TO-ENERGY
    Conversion: municipal solid waste combustion -> heat -> steam -> turbine
    Key vars: calorific value of waste, moisture, throughput (t/day)
    Fundamentals: mass-burn or RDF, flue-gas cleanup, Rankine cycle
